# Local scratch area for exercising the workspace packages by hand -- the place
# to write a throwaway script against `pfsmgraph.dataseq` and see what it does,
# without publishing to PyPI or waiting for a release.
#
# Deny-by-default, like the four import policies under `.scratch/`: nothing here
# is tracked unless it is named below. Everything you write in this directory is
# ignored, which is the point -- it is a workbench, not a source tree.
#
# The policy lives *here* rather than as a `/.notebooks/` line in the repo-root
# `.gitignore`, and that is load-bearing rather than stylistic. A directory
# ignored at the root is one git never descends into, so a nested `.gitignore`
# would never be consulted and the directory itself could not survive a clone --
# git tracks no empty directories. Tracking this file and the README is what
# makes the directory exist for anyone who checks the repo out.
#
# The repo-root `.gitignore` still applies underneath these rules, and is what
# keeps `__pycache__/`, `*.pyc`, `.ipynb_checkpoints`, `.DS_Store` and `.venv`
# out. Do not restate those here; a negation added below could re-admit them.
#
# The leading dot is deliberate, for the same reason `.scratch/` has one: it
# matches pytest's default `norecursedirs` entry `.*`, so `uv run pytest` does
# not collect anything written here. A directory named `notebooks/` would be
# walked, and a scratch file named `test_*.py` would join the real suite.
# The directory also sits outside `packages/`, so the `[tool.uv.workspace]`
# glob `packages/*` never claims it as a member.

# --- deny everything at this level -------------------------------------------
*

# The policy itself, and our own writing about the workbench. This negation is
# easy to forget and fails silently: a file written here without it is simply
# invisible to `git status`, so work looks committed and is not. That failure
# mode has caught out three of the four `.scratch/` imports -- see
# `docs/design/adr/0014-scratch-retention-and-per-package-scoping.md`.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
